/MarkupText (Motivated by how noradrenergic \(neuromodulatory\) bursts transiently increase neuronal gain under uncertainty, we introduce a dynamic gain scaling mechanism as a two-timescale optimization technique that balances adaptation and retention by modulating effective learning rates and flattening the local landscape through an effective reparameterization.)
/CA 1.0
/AP 113 0 R
/P 9 0 R
